menu "E-paper display application"

    config APP_SENSOR_NAME_PREFIX
        string "BLE advertised-name prefix of the Govee sensor"
        default "GV5171"
        help
            The sensor advertises as e.g. GV5171385C. The scanner does a
            case-insensitive substring match on this value.

    config APP_FULL_REFRESH_EVERY
        int "Full e-paper refresh every N display cycles"
        default 15
        range 1 1000
        help
            Number of display cycles between full e-paper refreshes.
            Partial refreshes are used on all other cycles to reduce
            flicker. The first refresh after boot is always a full one.

    config APP_SETUP_WINDOW_SEC
        int "Setup window after power-up (seconds)"
        default 300
        range 30 3600
        help
            After power-up (or a restart via a 5 s BOOT press) the device
            stays awake this long: the BLE clock service is advertised so the
            web page can set the clock, and the display updates on every
            sensor reading. Afterwards the deep-sleep cycle starts.

    config APP_WAKE_INTERVAL_SEC
        int "Deep-sleep wake interval (seconds)"
        default 60
        range 10 3600
        help
            The device wakes this often, waits for one sensor advertisement,
            updates the display and sleeps again. With a valid clock and an
            interval of 60 s the wakes are aligned to the start of a minute.

    config APP_WAKE_SCAN_TIMEOUT_MS
        int "Maximum BLE scan time per wake (ms)"
        default 8000
        range 1000 30000
        help
            If the sensor is not heard within this time the last values are
            shown again.

    config APP_SD_LOG_INTERVAL_SEC
        int "SD card log interval (seconds)"
        default 3600
        range 60 86400
        help
            A row is appended to the CSV file on the SD card at most this
            often, on the first cycle of each interval (aligned to the wall
            clock). Needs a valid clock.

    config APP_BLE_NAME
        string "BLE device name in setup mode"
        default "EPD-Uhr"
        help
            Name shown by the browser when the web page searches for the
            clock service.

    config APP_DEFAULT_TZ
        string "Default POSIX time zone"
        default "CET-1CEST,M3.5.0,M10.5.0/3"
        help
            Used until the web page sends a time zone. The default is
            Central European Time with daylight saving time.

endmenu
